[{"code":"pipe_rhs_not_application","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/parse/bad/PipeRhsNotApplication.beni","start":{"line":8,"col":11},"end":{"line":8,"col":12}},"title":"PIPE WITHOUT A CALL","message":"I was expecting a call after this `|>`, but I ran into `\\`.\n\n`x |> f a` is `f x a`: the value on the left becomes the FIRST argument of the call\non the right, so the right of `|>` must be that call — a function, or a call it is\none argument short of. A `let`, `if`, `case` or lambda has no argument list to\ninsert into. Parentheses do not hand it over as a value either — they are looked\nthrough, so `5 |> (\\y -> y + 1)` CALLS the lambda on `5` and is `6`. Write that if\nit is what you meant. When the block is the argument rather than the function, it\nbelongs on the right of `<|`, which does carry one: `f a <| case x of ...`."},{"code":"pipe_rhs_not_application","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/parse/bad/PipeRhsNotApplication.beni","start":{"line":12,"col":10},"end":{"line":12,"col":12}},"title":"PIPE WITHOUT A CALL","message":"I was expecting a call after this `|>`, but I ran into `if`.\n\n`x |> f a` is `f x a`: the value on the left becomes the FIRST argument of the call\non the right, so the right of `|>` must be that call — a function, or a call it is\none argument short of. A `let`, `if`, `case` or lambda has no argument list to\ninsert into. Parentheses do not hand it over as a value either — they are looked\nthrough, so `5 |> (\\y -> y + 1)` CALLS the lambda on `5` and is `6`. Write that if\nit is what you meant. When the block is the argument rather than the function, it\nbelongs on the right of `<|`, which does carry one: `f a <| case x of ...`."},{"code":"pipe_rhs_not_application","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/parse/bad/PipeRhsNotApplication.beni","start":{"line":16,"col":10},"end":{"line":16,"col":14}},"title":"PIPE WITHOUT A CALL","message":"I was expecting a call after this `|>`, but I ran into `case`.